  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:1em; border:1px solid #999; font-size:90%; text-align:center; background:#363636\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <td><i>This article details the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Jedi Academy Training Manual</a> Lightsaber Crystals type Ilum Crystals. For other uses, see <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ilum_(Disambiguation)\" title=\"Ilum (Disambiguation)\">Ilum (Disambiguation)</a>.</i> </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p><br> <i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p>The discovery of the planet <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ilum\" title=\"Ilum\">Ilum</a> was a landmark event in the history of the Jedi order. Up until its discovery, finding <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystals\">Lightsaber Crystals</a> to generate the full-strength blades that the Jedi order required could be tedious and time-consuming. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Mephite_Crystal\" title=\"Mephite Crystal\">Mephite Crystals</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pontite_Crystal\" title=\"Pontite Crystal\">Pontite Crystals</a> made for the best <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> blades, but even in the Adegan System, those <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystals\">Lightsaber Crystals</a> are rare. The discovery of Ilum brought with it entire caves filled with <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystals\">Lightsaber Crystals</a> whose structure was so similar to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Mephite_Crystal\" title=\"Mephite Crystal\">Mephite Crystals</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Pontite_Crystal\" title=\"Pontite Crystal\">Pontite Crystals</a> that the Jedi took them to be the same, at first. Jedi who undergo the ritual of <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Construction\" title=\"Lightsaber Construction\">Lightsaber Construction</a> seek out the caves of Ilum, as their <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystals\">Lightsaber Crystals</a> are considered the highest quality. </p><p>Ilum Crystals produce a full-strength <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> blade that is either blue or green in color. An Ilum Crystal grants the standard +1 bonus on attack rolls to its attuned wielder, common to most <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsabers\" title=\"Lightsabers\">Lightsabers</a>. </p>",
